<Layout title="Membership | Kin & Campus" description="Membership in a young adult wellness program for the college years in Blacksburg. August through May: chronic care, sick visits, forms, and academic-calendar check-ins. Membership is not insurance.">
<div class="w ph"><div class="eyebrow">Membership</div><h1>A membership they belong to for the school year.</h1><p class="lead">Kin &amp; Campus is membership in a unique young adult wellness program, built for the college years in Blacksburg. A board-certified pediatrician who lives here holds that year with them. What you are enrolling in is belonging: a place in a small program where chronic care does not lapse, the academic calendar is part of the medicine, and growing into adult health is the point of the year.</p></div>
<div class="w">
<div class="notes">
<div class="note-row"><h3>The year</h3><p>One student, August through May. The program stays small so the relationship can last the year. Nearby is how we see them in town. The membership is the thing they belong to.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>What belonging includes</h3><p>Chronic care that does not lapse: ADHD follow-up and refills, asthma, anxiety and depression medication, allergies, acne. Sick visits in Blacksburg. Virginia Tech, housing, and sports forms. Check-ins timed to move-in, finals, holidays, and the week after a break. Learning how to take care of themselves with a real doctor. Parents stay in the loop by agreement. The hometown doctor gets a note when the plan changes. A video visit when they do not need a room.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>What sits outside</h3><p>Emergency departments, hospital stays, specialty care, and advanced imaging are not part of membership. We help arrange them. Keep their primary insurance for labs, specialists, and hospital care. This website is not a medical chart.</p></div>
</div>

<div class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:56px">The academic calendar</div>
<h2>The year is shaped like campus life.</h2>
<p class="lead">Check-ins are not an extra courtesy. They are how a young adult wellness program works: the medicine follows the semester, so the plan still fits when the week gets loud.</p>
<div class="notes">
<div class="note-row"><h3>Move-in</h3><p>A first visit before classes take over, prescriptions transferred, immunization and housing paperwork in motion, and the sharing agreement written down.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>Holidays</h3><p>A look at what they actually took while they were home, and whether the plan still matches the person who came back.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>Finals</h3><p>Sleep, stress, asthma, ADHD, the refill they meant to request. We plan for that window on purpose.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>After a break</h3><p>The Sunday they return is when plans quietly lapse. Membership includes asking, in time, before the bottle is empty.</p></div>
</div>

<div class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:56px">When they should start with us</div>
<p class="lead">If it is a true emergency, call 911. The program is for the year they are growing into adult health, including the fever, the asthma flare, and the allergy a local pediatrician can handle. We already know their baseline. Members write us during the school year. This is not an around-the-clock line.</p>

<h2 style="margin:48px 0 20px">Questions parents ask</h2>
<details><summary>How does enrollment start?</summary><p>A parent usually writes first, and we schedule a conversation about the program. Once they join, the student meets their pediatrician in Blacksburg for an unhurried first visit, ideally before classes take over the week. From then, they belong to the program for the year.</p></details>
<details><summary>How soon can they be seen?</summary><p>During the school year we see members the same week, and usually the same day. The program stays small so that remains true when exams arrive. Availability is how a small membership holds the year during ordinary hours. For anything that cannot wait, call 911.</p></details>
<details><summary>Will you share my student's information with me?</summary><p>At 18 the chart is theirs. Before they join, we write down what they want you to hear, and we follow it. If the plan changes, their hometown doctor gets a note that afternoon. Belonging includes that agreement, so nobody is guessing in October.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does this replace insurance?</summary><p>No. Membership is not insurance. Keep their primary coverage for hospitalizations, emergency care, specialists, and labs. The program sits alongside that coverage and does the year of care insurance was never designed to hold.</p></details>
<details><summary>What if my student is away from Blacksburg?</summary><p>In-person care in Blacksburg is the center of the program. When they do not need a room, we can see them by video. The membership is still a local year, which is part of what makes it a program rather than a distant inbox.</p></details>
<details><summary>What if it's an emergency?</summary><p>Call 911 or go to the nearest emergency room. Once they are safe, tell us. We pick up the follow-up from there, and we write the hometown doctor if the plan has changed.</p></details>
<p style="margin-top:36px"><a class="btn" href={href("join")}>Join the program</a></p>
</div>
</Layout>
